      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "`outscript=VALUE:SCRIPT[:FLAGS]` only reads the flags when there are exactly three fields (bitcoin-tx.cpp:482). With a trailing or extra `:` the flags are silently dropped:\n\n```\n$ bitcoin-tx -create outscript=0:OP_DROP:S nversion=1\n010000000001000000000000000017a91471ed53322d470bb96657deb786b94f97dd46fb158700000000  # P2SH, as requested\n$ bitcoin-tx -create outscript=0:OP_DROP:S: nversion=1\n0100000000010000000000000000017500000000  # bare OP_DROP output, exit code 0\n```\n\nSo a typo gives a transaction paying to the raw script instead of the P2SH/P2WSH wrapper, with no error. `outpubkey` and `outaddr` already reject extra fields with \"TX output missing or too many separators\".\n\nThis rejects `outscript` arguments with more than three fields (\"TX output has too many separators\"). A case is added to `bitcoin-util-test.json`. It fails on master (exit code 0) and passes with the fix, and `tool_utils.py` passes.\n\nAI tools were used to help find this issue and to prepare the patch and test.\n",
